{
  "_about": "Abuse caps for the online economy (docs/orchestration/mmo/contracts.md sections 4 and 5). deposit_caps: units of one def an account may deposit into its vault per rolling 24 h. Each def's cap is the smallest category_caps value among its items.json categories (default deposit_default_cap); raw gathered bulk 2000, ores and metal 600, processed parts 200-1000, food 500, medicine 100, kits 20, tools and weapons 10, armour 5. A def missing from the table (added to items.json later, or one whose categories W2-DATA changes: flint, obsidian, peat) gets the same category rule at runtime (EconRules.deposit_cap), and deposit_default_cap only when no category matches; economy_tests checks the pinned table still follows the rule. Gathering still runs on the client in v1, so these caps bound what a cheating client can inject per day.",
  "max_open_listings": 50,
  "max_open_orders": 20,
  "max_vault_items": 500,
  "max_vault_pets": 100,
  "deposit_window_s": 86400,
  "deposit_default_cap": 200,
  "pet_species_cap": 3,
  "pet_daily_cap": 10,
  "denied_defs": [
    "tamed_animal"
  ],
  "allowed_flags": [
    "raw",
    "poisoned",
    "repacked",
    "flawless"
  ],
  "_repacked_about": "repacked: a kit back from pack-up (build_placer.gd) places without construction XP. It trades with the flag, so the buyer places it without XP as the seller would have.",
  "refused_flags": [
    "locked",
    "unstable"
  ],
  "level_min": 1,
  "level_max": 60,
  "process_count_max": 99,
  "pet_stat_tolerance": 0.005,
  "instance_fields": {
    "_about": "Per-instance fields a server bag row carries besides its provenance stamp (uid, origin, seq): ItemStack.to_dict writes creator and created_at for every instance with a uid, which W2-INV gives every material and food unit, and W2-PROCESS carries both through an in-place step. Escrow keeps them byte for byte; this only bounds their type. Anything else is refused at deposit.",
